{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f305c413e0ad9b03","type":"text","text":"[[Dolor Matris]]\n#DolorMatris","x":-680,"y":-620,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a29bd1a22c97f852","x":-840,"y":-520,"width":480,"height":500,"type":"text","text":"1. The Emerald Chamber of Denial:\n\n- **The Scene:** The room is opulent and perfectly safe-looking, filled with pleasant emerald light. Five ornate, glowing emerald levers sit on pedestals in the center of the room. The exit door is shut.\n    \n- **The Trap:** An invisible, odorless, magical poison is slowly filling the room (players must make increasingly difficult Constitution saving throws every minute). Pulling the ornate emerald levers does nothing but trigger a pleasant chime.\n    \n- **The Solution:** The party must deny the obvious \"perfect\" solution and look for the ugly truth. Hidden in the dark, dusty corners of the room are five rusted, jagged iron levers. They are painful to touch (dealing 1d4 piercing damage). To open the door, all five players must accept the painful truth and pull the five iron levers simultaneously, ignoring the alluring emerald illusions."},
		{"id":"cdddd5fcb6f074bf","x":-840,"y":55,"width":500,"height":565,"type":"text","text":"3. The Saphire Chamber of Bargaining:\n\n- **The Scene:** A sterile, quiet room with a massive set of jeweler's scales blocking the exit, balanced by a giant sapphire. Five small offering bowls sit in front of the scales. A magical voice states: _\"Trade a piece of your power for passage.\"_\n    \n- **The Trap:** The scale does not accept gold, mundane items, or standard magical gear. It only accepts personal vitality or potential.\n    \n- **The Solution:** To tip the master scale, each of the five players must simultaneously place a mechanical sacrifice into their respective bowl. This requires giving up something mechanical until their next long rest: expending their highest-level spell slot, giving up half their total Hit Dice, taking a level of Exhaustion, or permanently sacrificing a cherished trinket from their backstory. Only when all five have bargained away a piece of themselves will the sapphire shatter and the door open."},
		{"id":"bdcc1b466a61abf1","x":-283,"y":-683,"width":460,"height":93,"type":"text","text":"denial, anger, bargaining, depression, and acceptance"},
		{"id":"86dbfbee8e4d0ddc","x":-307,"y":-520,"width":507,"height":505,"type":"text","text":"2. The Ruby Chamber of Anger:\n3. \n- **The Scene:** The room is scorching hot, lit by a pulsing ruby crystal in the ceiling. Five pressure plates surround the locked exit door. Standing between the players and the plates are five animated Obsidian Golems.\n    \n- **The Trap:** Whenever a player attacks a Golem, the room's temperature spikes, dealing fire damage to everyone, and the Golem heals or duplicates. Any aggressive action (spells, attacks, forced movement) fuels the room's anger.\n    \n- **The Solution:** Pacifism and endurance. The players must realize they cannot fight their way out. Each of the five players must walk past the Golems, stand on a pressure plate, and willingly take the Dodge action for three consecutive rounds while the Golems attack them. By absorbing the blows and refusing to strike back, the ruby's glow fades, the Golems crumble to dust, and the door opens."},
		{"id":"6a276329f34efa2e","x":-567,"y":700,"width":627,"height":580,"type":"text","text":"5. The Diamond Chamber of Acceptance:\n\n- **The Scene:** A bright, brilliantly lit room containing a flawless diamond pedestal. Beyond it is the exit door, which is already wide open, revealing the outside world or the next dungeon tier. However, a shimmering, translucent barrier blocks the archway.\n    \n- **The Trap:** There is no trap, and there are no enemies. Any spell cast at the barrier dissipates. Any weapon swung at it bounces off. If a player tries to force their way through, they are gently repelled.\n    \n- **The Solution:** To pass through the barrier, the players must let go. They must lay down all their weapons, drop their spellcasting focuses, and unequip their shields, placing them on the diamond pedestal. They must approach the barrier entirely vulnerable and state one thing their character has learned or accepted during the dungeon dive. Once they accept their vulnerability, the barrier allows them to simply walk through. Their gear is magically teleported to their bags once they are safely on the other side."},
		{"id":"5f8fba4150269dcc","x":-277,"y":55,"width":537,"height":565,"type":"text","text":"4. The Obsidian Chamber of Depression:\n\n- **The Scene:** The room is plunged into magical darkness that even darkvision struggles to pierce. The air is incredibly heavy, halving everyone's movement speed. There are five massive, incredibly heavy obsidian spheres scattered around the room, and five recessed divots near the exit.\n    \n- **The Trap:** The spheres are too heavy for even a barbarian to move alone (DC 30 Athletics). The magical atmosphere creates a sense of isolation; voices are muffled, and players cannot easily see each other. If players try to act alone, they fail and take psychic damage from the overwhelming lethargy.\n    \n- **The Solution:** They must literally carry the weight together. The players must find each other in the dark and link up. By taking the Help action to assist a single pusher, the DC lowers significantly. All five players must group up and push one sphere at a time together, moving slowly as a single unit to slot all five spheres into the divots."}
	],
	"edges":[]
}